+PR36 copied-center schedule: independent bounded mathematical audit
+Source commit: 11817ccacb564bb7f98789c20dc11d3fece207e3
+
+Conclusion: the written copied-center identity is valid under the stated
+terminal-output-use and paid complete-stream copy interface. It preserves
+arbitrary dirty values in BOTH invocation orientations. It is a genuine
+rank saving in the changed physical call list, not removal of the separately
+paid endpoint correction. No new local schedule obstruction was found.
+This is not a complete independent verification of the new producer,
+complex residual compiler, physical basis theorem or analytic/tape interfaces.
+
+General identity (no finite test is needed for this algebra)
+Let F_Q denote the invertible address frame and let the original terminal
+hold F_U w. The vector w is the entire arbitrary scalar value, including
+all old scratch contributions. For forward schedule U -> 0 -> 1, the old
+scatter source is F_0 w and the old cleanup input is F_1 w. The new schedule
+copies F_U w, applies F_0 F_U^-1 to the copy, uses it for every read-only
+scatter, and discards it. On the retained original it applies F_1 F_U^-1.
+Both vectors are exactly the old ones. Hence any later cleanup gates,
+source-copy cancellation and endpoint operator receive identical inputs.
+
+For reverse complementary schedule 0 -> 1 -> Uperp, first advance the
+original from F_0 w to F_Uperp w; copy that and apply F_1 F_Uperp^-1.
+The scatter sees F_1 w and cleanup sees F_Uperp w, exactly as before.
+This does not require w to be a fresh producer output or the scratch to be
+zero. A subsequent arbitrary linear mixer cannot distinguish the schedules.
+It also holds with spectator fields and suppressed tensor factors untouched.
+
+In the orthogonal decomposition D0 plus active local F_h, the old ranks
+are (r,h) forward and (h,r) reverse. The new copied change has rank r
+and the direct original change rank h-r. Partial swaps are involutions.
+For phases, forward copied change is C_U^-1, reverse copied change C_U,
+and direct original change is C_Uperp. These are separately PAID recursive
+calls, so the new local profile is z^r+z^(h-r), with rank saving r.
+The inverse phase must not be silently replaced by a forward phase.
+
+Terminal separation is necessary, and the inspected compiler supplies it:
+- notes/copied-centers-lemma.tex:9-13 states the terminal contract.
+- scripts/partial_swap/match_positive_dag.cpp:21-28 creates a separate
+  high-bit-tagged output-use vertex for each root occurrence. Only addition
+  nodes are donor/left vertices; terminal uses are right vertices and have
+  no later producer consumer. Matching may enter but cannot exit a terminal.
+- scripts/endpoint_gauge/match_complex_general.cpp:16-29 does the same for
+  the complex carrier graph. Roots that also have internal producer uses
+  do not identify their distinct terminal output-use with those other uses.
+- scripts/structured_bulk/complex.py:107-111 appends the h-d doubled centers
+  and d coordinate-disjoint centers as distinct designated output uses;
+  its histogram code:184-196 separately records the rank-r/rank-h detour.
+The identity would NOT apply without further accounting to an arbitrary
+middle producer node that still changes value or controls later producer
+operations during the proposed jump. The existing terminal separation is
+therefore a real proof condition, not merely the aggregate histogram test.
+
+Cost and new rank mass
+Every temporary duplicates precisely one original role stream at volume V/W.
+Paureel's retained interface pays copy/read/discard O(V/W), parks originals,
+and processes one extra stream sequentially on the same depth-first tapes;
+see references/copied-centers/pr29/paureel-direct-transfer.tex:78-88 and
+notes/copied-centers-lemma.tex:29-35. The r-child on the temporary is included;
+there is no uncharged undo or extra independently varying row coordinate.
+With h codimension-one centers, each saves h-1, hence saves ell_h=h(h-1).
+H'_1=H_1+h and H'_h=H_h-h, with H'_(h-1)=H_(h-1) unchanged. Applying both
+axis banks saves L=v_b ell_a+v_a ell_b, so s=Wm-N+L. All N rank-one data
+endpoint-copy calls remain charged. Swapping axis order does not affect this
+local proof, role-volume argument, or the total L; reversal23/25 still needs
+its own actual common-basis/corner profile, which this audit does not supply.
+
+Complex endpoint check
+notes/copied-centers-complex.tex:34-55 has source frames(T,I), terminal(F,E),
+E=F T^-1. Applying the scalar shear matrix(-y,x+y) therefore yields
+A=-F y and B=F T^-2 x+E y. Retain A, apply T^-1 to a COPY and add it to B;
+T^-1 A=-E y, leaving F T^-2 x. This costs one rank-one inverse child per
+pair. It is not zero-cost and does not alter A. Since T^2=X_u and u has
+weight nine, F T^-2 has C^-1 on those nine coordinates and C elsewhere.
+The coordinate identity i Z C^-1 Z=C gives the paid scalar/diagonal wrappers
+i^(9f) Z_u (F T^-2) Z_u=F on f columns. Negation restores A to F y, and
+undoing the bank exchange yields the two required full-F outputs.
+The translated auxiliary endpoint(C_I C_D0) C_D0^-1=C_I is unchanged.
+General nondegenerate/alternating residual compilation remains inherited
+from the cited Gauss normal-form theorem, not proved by these small tests.
+
+Precision integration requirement
+PR36 changes E to64(W_c+m_c+G+1)^3, with G the NEW literal grouped scalar
+upper charge including two extra local groups per copied center and one
+endpoint-addition group per pair. Recompute rather than reuse old E/C0.
+The written checks E>literal, 2B(m-r)>=s+E, C0>2B+18 support the same
+completed-child C1=1 induction. The old indefinite/balanced_assembly.py
+was intentionally pinned to E=64(W+m+1)^3; an explicit attributed formula
+adaptation is required for this new graph. A fixed beta1/20 remains legal
+with leaf saving(19/20)*71.7e-6 exceeding the proposed bit saving; numerical
+constraints and all eventual thresholds must be recomputed for actual data.
+
+Independent exact controls
+copied_center_operator_audit.py imports NO PR36 implementation and uses
+Fraction pairs for exact Gaussian dyadics. It tests every center basis vector
+and dirty vectors, both orientations, arbitrary dirty scatter targets,
+multiple scalar reads and subsequent cleanup incidence. Results:
+ 514 bit partial-swap cases (four address directions, nonzero background),
+ 34 Gaussian phase center cases, and33 phase endpoint cases, including
+ an exact literal weight-nine diagonal identity on a dirty512-vector.
+These confirm local algebra and sign conventions, not general geometry or
+the whole fixed-tape machine. The general argument above is what transfers
+to all physical occurrences and arbitrary allowed bases.
+
+Attribution: copied retained-center construction icekylinx PR36; copy/retain/
+transform/discard interface Aurel Prosz(Paureel), inherited through Zhihao
+Chen PR29; original scalar/compiler and semantic framework retain the PR36
+source attributions. Existing local endpoint-obstruction experiments assumed
+an unchanged center schedule and do not rule out this distinct construction.
