+PR34 balanced assembly: bounded independent source audit
+
+Conclusion: the replacement of original prefix saving 1-epsilon(1+c) by
+1-epsilon is justified CONDITIONALLY by a changed, paid physical layout,
+combined with the separately supplied arbitrary-coordinate router and bulk
+resampling construction. I found no additional transfer obstruction for the
+PR34 bit-interchange adapter. This is not an independent proof of all inherited
+all-size tape, analytic, finite-basis, or prime/setup hypotheses, and not a full
+review of PR34 or its numerical certificate.
+
+Source correspondence
+The following local files in integer-mult-bounds-two-stage-dimensions-review
+were compared byte-for-byte against origin/pr34 (head 7fecbe3) in stream-review:
+references/rad20/reports/review-balanced-transform.md
+ sha256 0c3a5b6f17188205d35cd421ef0c35c71f6111698f497e89da3ef7f870fef862
+references/rad20/reports/downstream-semantic-bulk-assembly.md
+ sha256 ccdeaeac7c6a1c08483fea2285a7d089d782f2c18b7be867c3fc9f77457637fd
+references/rad20/reports/review-arbitrary-routing.md
+ sha256 f18f535a096abae473db71a4ae3f275d0116d7438fb18594d5b160571db670fd
+references/rad20/reports/review-bulk-resampling.md
